<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Battle of Kosovo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1448">1448</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-hungarian-wars">Ottoman–Hungarian wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Battle of Kosovo was fought on 17–20 October 1448 on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> plain, where the Ottoman army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii">Murad II</a> defeated a Hungarian and Wallachian army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-hunyadi">John Hunyadi</a>. It ended Hunyadi's hope of reversing the defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varna">Varna</a>, and on his retreat he was briefly held captive by the Serbian despot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durad-brankovic">Đurađ Branković</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-battle-of-kosovo.jpg" alt="Second Battle of Kosovo" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sueleymanname_akinci.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
